The long diagnostic has exposed an important command-selection issue, not a proof defect: selecting only `SPEC.get-odd-collatz` removes the `collatz-loop` circularity it depends on, so the prover unrolls indefinitely. The generation trace itself recorded the same entry-only problem. I’m terminating that diagnostic and will run the valid independent targets: the loop claim alone, then the complete spec (which includes the loop claim as the entry theorem’s auxiliary circularity).
